{"name":"Sinister Minister","hex":"#353331","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sinister","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Inauspicious, ominous, unlucky, illegitimate.","Evil or seemingly evil; indicating lurking danger or harm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sinister"},{"term":"minister","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is trained to preach, to perform religious ceremonies, and to afford pastoral care at a Protestant church.","A person (either a layperson or an ordained clergy member) who is commissioned to perform some act on behalf of the Catholic Church."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To attend to (the needs of); to tend; to take care (of); to give aid; to give service.","To function as a clergyman or as the officiant in church worship."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minister"}],"entries":[{"title":"Béla Fleck and the Flecktones (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Béla Fleck and the Flecktones is the debut album by Béla Fleck and the Flecktones, released in 1990. It reached number 17 on the Billboard Top Contemporary Jazz Albums chart. At the Grammy Awards of 1997, a live version of \"The Sinister Minister\", a track from the album, won the Best Pop Instrumental Performance award."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/B%C3%A9la_Fleck_and_the_Flecktones_%28B%C3%A9la_Fleck_and_the_Flecktones_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A9la_Fleck_and_the_Flecktones_(album)"},{"title":"Father James Mitchell","blocks":[{"text":"James Lamar Mitchell is an American professional wrestling manager, known for his appearances with World Championship Wrestling (WCW) as James Vandenberg, Extreme Championship Wrestling (ECW) as The Sinister Minister, and Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA) under his own name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Mr._Mitchell_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Mr._Mitchell_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Father_James_Mitchell"},{"title":"Sinister Minister (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Sinister Minister is a thoroughbred race horse. As a foal born on March 29, 2003, he was a possible contender for the American Triple Crown in 2006."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/%E7%A8%AE%E7%89%A1%E9%A6%AC%E6%99%82%E4%BB%A3%E3%81%AE%E3%82%B7%E3%83%8B%E3%82%B9%E3%82%BF%E3%83%BC%E3%83%9F%E3%83%8B%E3%82%B9%E3%82%BF%E3%83%BC%282020%E5%B9%B410%E6%9C%88%E6%92%AE%E5%BD%B1%29.jpg/330px-%E7%A8%AE%E7%89%A1%E9%A6%AC%E6%99%82%E4%BB%A3%E3%81%AE%E3%82%B7%E3%83%8B%E3%82%B9%E3%82%BF%E3%83%BC%E3%83%9F%E3%83%8B%E3%82%B9%E3%82%BF%E3%83%BC%282020%E5%B9%B410%E6%9C%88%E6%92%AE%E5%BD%B1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinister_Minister_(horse)"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"sinister":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/En-us-sinister.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/59/En-us-sinister.ogg/En-us-sinister.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/En-au-sinister.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/61/En-au-sinister.ogg/En-au-sinister.ogg.mp3"}],"minister":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/En-us-minister.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/En